From: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: stdio.h: use __builtin_va_arg_pack only where the compiler has it

clang has no __builtin_va_arg_pack, so building with these headers
failed in the snprintf and sprintf wrappers ("use of unknown builtin").
Define those two wrappers only when the compiler provides the builtin;
with clang the other wrappers stay in place. GCC is not affected: it
has the builtin, and the same program builds to an identical binary
with and without this change.

Signed-off-by: liviyifan <344781483+liviyifan@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/include/stdio.h
+++ b/include/stdio.h
@@ -92,6 +92,8 @@
 	return __r;
 }
 
+/* __builtin_va_arg_pack is GCC only (not in clang) */
+#if __has_builtin(__builtin_va_arg_pack)
 _FORTIFY_FN(snprintf) int snprintf(char *__s, size_t __n, const char *__f, ...)
 {
 	size_t __b = __builtin_object_size(__s, 0);
@@ -121,6 +123,7 @@
 	return __r;
 #pragma GCC diagnostic pop
 }
+#endif
 
 #ifdef __cplusplus
 }
